                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I can easily recommend this game if you're someone who went \"oh wow\" and had to take some time to think after playing Dear Esther; otherwise, I'm afraid it can be very slow and a bit awkward to get through at times.\nI'd categorize this more as interactive fiction than a game, so don't expect much besides walking and clicking. \n(Walking speed is pretty slow. I sprinted throughout the entirety of the game.)\n\nAll things, especially the fact that this is over 10 years old, considered, I think Fragments of Him depicts how confusing it can be to lose a loved one rather well.\n\nIf you've lost a loved one, have 10 bucks, about 2 hours, and an open mind, I'd give this game a shot.",
